            <ArticleTitle>The duration of pain relief after penile block to boys undergoing circumcision.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>432-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bupivacaine plain, 2.5 mg/ml, was used for a nerve block of the dorsal nerves of the penis. Satisfactory postoperative analgesia was obtained in 24 of 28 boys undergoing circumcision. Eighteen of the 24 boys with a successful nerve block did not require analgesics during the first 24 h postoperatively. All blocks were performed by the surgeon just before surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
